      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:2:14",
      "text": [
        " أَيُّمَا مُؤْمِنٍ حَافَظَ عَلَى الصَّلَوَاتِ الْمَفْرُوضَةِ فَصَلَّاهَا لِوَقْتِهَا فَلَيْسَ هَذَا مِنَ الْغَافِلِينَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father from Ibn Mahboub, from Jameel Bin Darraj, from one of his companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Whichever Believers is preserving upon the Obligatory <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>, so he prays these upon their (Prescribed) timings, so this one is not from the oblivious (unaware) ones’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "14. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn Mahbub from Jamil ibn Darraj from certain persons of his people who has said the following: “Abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Whoever of the believers preserves his obligatory Salah (prayers) and performs them in time, he is not of the neglectful people.’” "
        ]
      }
